import DifferentialGeometry.PDE.RicciFlow.DeTurck.ShortTime

/-!
# Recovery of the Ricci flow from the DeTurck flow

The **DeTurck flow** `∂_t g = -2 Ric(g) + ℒ_{V(g)} g` is strictly parabolic
and admits a short-time-existence theorem
(`DifferentialGeometry.PDE.RicciFlow.DeTurck.deTurckFlow_shortTime_exists`).
The **Ricci flow** `∂_t g = -2 Ric(g)` itself is only weakly parabolic, due
to the diffeomorphism gauge invariance of the Ricci tensor.

**DeTurck's recovery construction** bridges the two. Given a DeTurck flow
`g_⋅ : ℝ → SmoothRiemannianMetric I M` with background `g₀`, define the
**diffeomorphism flow** `φ_⋅ : ℝ → M → M` as the integral flow of the
time-dependent vector field

  `V_t := -deTurckVF g₀ (g_⋅ t)`.

Then the pull-back `t ↦ φ_t^* (g_⋅ t)` is a solution of the original
Ricci flow with initial value `g₀`. This is the diffeomorphism-gauge
transformation that undoes the DeTurck modification.

## Main definitions and theorems

* `deTurckDiffeomorphismFlow` — the diffeomorphism flow `φ_⋅` of the
  time-dependent vector field `V_t = -deTurckVF g₀ (g_⋅ t)` generated by
  a DeTurck-flow solution `g_⋅`.
* `IsRicciFlow g₀ T g_⋅` — the predicate that a one-parameter family of
  metrics is a solution of the Ricci flow `∂_t g = -2 Ric(g)` on
  `[0, T]` with initial value `g₀`.
* `deTurckInverse_isRicciFlow` — given a DeTurck flow with background
  `g₀`, there exists a Ricci flow with the same initial value `g₀`,
  obtained as the pull-back of `g_⋅` along
  `deTurckDiffeomorphismFlow`.

In the skeleton:

* `deTurckDiffeomorphismFlow` is the trivial identity flow `fun _ x => x`;
* `IsRicciFlow` is the trivial predicate `True`;
* `deTurckInverse_isRicciFlow` records the existence of a Ricci-flow
  solution given a DeTurck-flow solution, with the trivial constant
  witness `fun _ => g₀`.

Downstream files refine `deTurckDiffeomorphismFlow` to the genuine
integral flow of the time-dependent vector field, `IsRicciFlow` to the
precise time-derivative equation `∂_t g_t = -2 Ric(g_t)`, and
`deTurckInverse_isRicciFlow` to the statement that the pull-back of any
DeTurck flow along its diffeomorphism flow satisfies the Ricci flow.
-/

noncomputable section

set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
